[Music]  what's up everybody it's elbow geo 208  coming at you with the iron Lords  podcast dream team today we're going to  be reviewing a new game called hyper jam  brought to you by bit dragon I like to  say thank you to bit dragon for sending  us a copy to review I review this copy  on Xbox one X it's kind of hard to  categorize this shooter hack and slash  Battle Royale style game  it's 80s cyberpunk feel lots of color  lots of lasers the character is a very  fluid jumping around moving from side to  side very fun game to play there's about  eight different maps you can play on all  of them fairly small you're only playing  with two to four players either online  or couch co-op and each map has  different aspects to it  some have waterfalls some have walls  that open some have cover that will  appear for you or floors that will drop  out making each match difficult you play  in three rounds to the death whoever has  the most whoever gets to the most points  wins so you go around at the round and  whoever gets to the most points first  and then survives that next wave ends up  being the victor the coolest part about  this game is probably the cards that you  get ability cards at the beginning each  round some allow you to have different  punches as far as fire or freezing or  you can disorient to do  other players with your attacks or you  can move faster there's a card where you  are gaining health as the match goes on  so you'll just continue to regain your  health and then there's a card that  allows you to I guess be like a Titan so  you have reduced strength or increased  strength rather and reduce fall damage  things like that and all these cards can  be stacked the biggest takeaway from the  cards is that whoever loses the game has  first pick so those first couple of  rounds is more advantageous to not be  the winner because then you'll be able  to get the best pick of the cards those  last matches especially if you have a  p-card stack it's crucial to have like  health stacked a few times so that  you're constantly regaining health or  that you can disorient your other  victims with your attacks because then  as soon as they get hit they can't  though they might just fall off the map  which is very very advantageous if  you're trying to complete the  achievement for winning a match without  using any weapons I was actually able to  get that while reviewing this game and  that was one of my biggest advances for  getting that achievement was to be able  to have that disorient card and the  health card unknown it's a great game  one of the fallbacks I did have with it  was finding an online match at one time  the one time that I did find out online  match it took me about 15 to 20 minutes  to find a person so my best bet with  this game is to do couch co-op or to  have a team of players that you already  know they have this game to be able to  match up with  but it's a lot of fun a lot of fun cool  music cool graphics it's not a  photorealistic game so if that's what  you're looking for this is not that game  for you but I enjoyed it I had a lot of  fun I got through some achievements if  your achievement hunter you're gonna  handle it enjoy this game you'll be able  to knock most of the achievements out in  a few hours and yeah I loved it it was  cool cool game I can't wait to see more  from bit dragon and once again thank you  so much  bit dragon for letting us review this  game for you iron Lords podcast greatly  appreciate your generosity and thank you  everybody for coming to listen to the  review you guys can catch our lures  podcast Sundays check the Twitter follow  everybody it'll be on YouTube Sunday  mornings these guys are on East Coast  time so it's gonna be a little early for  us West Coast people but greatly  appreciate everybody that comes by and  gives us the support thank you again  peace  [Music]

